-- title:
--   Freeness of the Cartier module of a height-h formal group
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a perfect field of characteristic $p$ (a field with `CharP k p` and `PerfectRing k p`), let $d$ be a natural number, and let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $k$ in the sense of [`MvFormalGroup d k`](def/MvFormalGroup_BasicV2.html#L15): a family of $d$ power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, whose linear coefficients in each of the two groups of variables are the Kronecker delta, and which satisfies the associativity identity under substitution; assume moreover that $\Phi$ is commutative, i.e. interchanging the two groups of variables leaves each component unchanged. Let $h$ be a natural number, and assume that the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ (formally, `MvPowerSeries (Fin d) k`) by the ideal generated by the $d$ components of $\Phi.\mathrm{nthSeries}\ p$ — the $p$-fold iterate of the group law, obtained by substituting the $(p-1)$-fold iterate and the variables themselves into $\Phi$, so the components of the $[p]$-series — has $k$-dimension exactly $p^h$. The conclusion is that the type of bases of [`MvFormalGroup.CartierModule p Φ`](def/MvFormalGroup_CartierModule.html#L162) indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,h$ over the Witt vectors $W(k)$ is nonempty; here the Cartier module consists of the $d$-tuples of power series in countably many variables with zero constant term which are additive with respect to the Witt addition polynomials in the sense recorded by `subst_eq`, with its $W(k)$-module structure. Thus the Cartier module is free of rank $h$ over $W(k)$.
--
--   This is the structure theorem for the Cartier–Dieudonné module of a $p$-divisible commutative formal group of height $h$ over a perfect field of characteristic $p$, in the covariant normalisation by homomorphisms from the formal Witt group, the height being encoded by the $k$-dimension $p^h$ of the algebra cut out by the $[p]$-series. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where the Cartier module of a special formal $O_D$-module is decomposed by means of an explicit pair of basis-like generators.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_CartierModule_nonempty_basis_of_finrank_eq_pow.lean

